{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794363551136,"sessionID":"ses_e37993df6ffeDue0pJSjzMGtzF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_ff9cc65c74274e78812d932a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"ls -R /workspace | head -60; echo ---; cat /workspace/README.md 2>/dev/null"},"output":"/workspace:\nDockerfile\nREADME.md\nbackend\nfrontend\n\n/workspace/backend:\napp.py\nrequirements.lock\nrequirements.txt\n\n/workspace/frontend:\nindex.html\npackage-lock.json\npackage.json\nsrc\nvite.config.ts\n\n/workspace/frontend/src:\nApp.tsx\nmain.tsx\n---\n# App\n\n## Run contract\n\n- The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n- The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n- The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n- Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n\n## Layout\n\n- `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n- `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n\nDependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n","metadata":{"output":"/workspace:\nDockerfile\nREADME.md\nbackend\nfrontend\n\n/workspace/backend:\napp.py\nrequirements.lock\nrequirements.txt\n\n/workspace/frontend:\nindex.html\npackage-lock.json\npackage.json\nsrc\nvite.config.ts\n\n/workspace/frontend/src:\nApp.tsx\nmain.tsx\n---\n# App\n\n## Run contract\n\n- The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n- The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n- The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n- Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n\n## Layout\n\n- `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n- `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n\nDependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"ls -R /workspace | head -60; echo ---; cat /workspace/README.md 2>/dev/null","time":{"start":1794363551002,"end":1794363551077}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c866ecf60019lMJqDYO0bYjJ5","sessionID":"ses_e37993df6ffeDue0pJSjzMGtzF","messageID":"msg_1c866e29e001rpIjqUlr5IU3u1"}}
